id: pm-9aaji6
title: Linked pm test children inherit production Sentry environment and turn sandbox failures into release-blocking incidents
description: "PM-CLI-31 is a single high unresolved event whose timestamp exactly matches the failed linked-test run test-local-mspeooe4-5ujujx on pm-cg1sjb. The linked pnpm lint child ran against a seeded tracker sandbox, raised the expected missing assurance-gate negative signal, but inherited no SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT override so the CLI defaulted to production and polluted the fail-closed release inventory. Linked-test orchestration must default child Sentry classification to test while preserving explicit test-authored overrides."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-12T02:47:19.822Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-12T04:37:02.878Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-12T03:58:30.649Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-12T03:58:30.649Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Every linked-test child defaults SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT to test before run-level and per-test directives; an explicit linked-test SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT override remains possible; the regression executes through the real runTest child boundary; PM-CLI-31 is documented and dispositioned without hiding genuine production faults; full strict gates remain green
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
resolution: "Linked pm test children now default to the test Sentry environment before explicit run-level and per-test directives, preventing sandbox failures from polluting production diagnostics."
expected_result: Default linked children classify as test; run-level and per-test overrides retain deterministic precedence; production Sentry sees no sandbox-negative events.
actual_result: "Merged PR #986 proves default, run-level, and per-test precedence through real child processes; PM-CLI-31 was resolved in the next release and the live 14-day gate is 0 critical/0 high."
